From: rmuxnet <armandas.kvietkus@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 25 Apr 2026 20:21:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ps4: fix power button input teardown
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary="------------false"

This is a multi-part message in MIME format.
--------------false
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8; format=fixed
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit


The PS4 ICC power-button driver allocates an input device and registers
it with input_register_device(). Once registration succeeds, teardown
must use input_unregister_device(); input_free_device() is only valid for
the pre-registration failure path.

Use input_unregister_device() in icc_pwrbutton_remove() and keep the
existing input_register_device() failure path unchanged.

Power-button event reporting and ICC notification commands are unchanged.

Signed-off-by: rmuxnet <armandas.kvietkus@proton.me>
---
 drivers/ps4/ps4-apcie-pwrbutton.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)


--------------false
Content-Type: text/x-patch; name="0076-ps4-fix-power-button-input-teardown.patch"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
Content-Disposition: attachment; filename="0076-ps4-fix-power-button-input-teardown.patch"

diff --git a/drivers/ps4/ps4-apcie-pwrbutton.c b/drivers/ps4/ps4-apcie-pwrbutton.c
index 0fef75c4aae67edbda4c9d2d2f9741c6357765c3..af0f12add6adc6f69e36b14bad60c5c27055ba63 100644
--- a/drivers/ps4/ps4-apcie-pwrbutton.c
+++ b/drivers/ps4/ps4-apcie-pwrbutton.c
@@ -70,6 +70,6 @@ int icc_pwrbutton_init(struct apcie_dev *sc)
 void icc_pwrbutton_remove(struct apcie_dev *sc)
 {
 	if (sc->icc.pwrbutton_dev)
-		input_free_device(sc->icc.pwrbutton_dev);
+		input_unregister_device(sc->icc.pwrbutton_dev);
 	sc->icc.pwrbutton_dev = NULL;
 }

--------------false--


